From 4bf9ee7ef69a79c6338474f8a58c83dc682abb19 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 18:07:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Train B, worker 6 (X11): exchanging life, damage by each,
 connive, monstrosity, prepare, a block trigger

Engine pieces, each built once and generally:
- exchangeLife (CR 701.12): a life total with a creature's toughness (layer 7b) or with another
  player's, all or nothing.
- damageEach (Forge's EachDamage): each of a set deals damage counted for itself, to itself or
  to targets; in the damage-order question too.
- connive (CR 701.50): each permanent connives in turn, the APNAP player choosing which next;
  the draw, the discard and a counter per nonland card; "each creature that convoked this
  spell" (the cast records its convokers).
- alterAttribute: monstrous (CR 701.37, monstrosity N) and prepared (CR 722.3: the prepare
  spell's copy in exile, castable by the permanent's controller, unprepared as it is cast).
- "enters prepared", an entering replacement (CR 614.1c); a preparation card's `prepare` face.
- Triggers "blocks" (CR 509.3a-b) and "becomes monstrous"; a scenario `block` step.
- Target specs: distinctFrom ("other", "a second"), onlyIf (a target had only if cast in your
  main phase, CR 601.2c), differentControllers (refused with instructions; both pilots keep it).
- A mana value at most a counted amount (life you lost this turn).
- Credits: AlternateAdditionalCost (built before, no new code), ETBReplacement, Monstrosity,
  LifeYouLostThisTurn, IfCastInOwnMainPhase.

Cards: Demand Answers, Stir Up Trouble, Return to Dust, Smuggler's Copter, Lethal Scheme,
Protector of the Wastes, Betor, Ancestor's Voice, Tree of Perdition, Tree of Redemption, Wave
of Reckoning, Goblin Glasswright // Craft with Pride. Not defined: Ichormoon Gauntlet and
Tidus, Yuna's Guardian (addTurn, moveCounters and the counter-kind question unfinished,
reverted). The suites that used exchangeLife as the unbuilt example now use addTurn.

check-cards: 1625 definitions, 2552 scenarios, 0 failed. engine-cards, engine-compile,
engine-vocabulary, engine-overload, engine-repeat, engine-rules-conformance, game-replay,
data-integrity and feature-wiring pass. Generated files regenerated.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
